avcodec/audiotoolboxdec: decode again after a flush that follows the end

goffmpeg #103. Upstream: not submitted yet.

An empty packet, the end of the stream, sets eof, and from then on the
input callback hands AudioToolbox no packets. Flushing reset the
converter and dropped the held packets, but kept eof, so a decoder that
had been drained gave no audio after avcodec_flush_buffers and a seek.
A player that loops, or seeks back after the end, went silent, and one
that paces video by the audio clock stalled with it.

Measured on macOS 27: decoding an AAC-LC M4A to the end with the drain,
flushing, seeking to 0 and decoding again gave 0 samples the second
time with aac_at and the full count with FFmpeg's aac. On an iPad (10th
generation), a 4 s clip looping in a player rendered 1.6 frames a
second instead of 24. The flush now clears eof. With it, the second
pass gives the full count with aac_at for AAC-LC, HE-AAC and HE-AACv2
M4A and AAC-LC ADTS.

diff --git a/libavcodec/audiotoolboxdec.c b/libavcodec/audiotoolboxdec.c
index 0e90d64b74..be2f788d5a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/audiotoolboxdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/audiotoolboxdec.c
@@ -687,6 +687,7 @@ static av_cold void ffat_decode_flush(AVCodecContext *avctx)
     AudioConverterReset(at->converter);
     av_packet_unref(&at->new_in_pkt);
     av_packet_unref(&at->in_pkt);
+    at->eof = 0;
 }
 
 static av_cold int ffat_close_decoder(AVCodecContext *avctx)
